            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A user equipment (200) comprising: a selector (210) configured to select, in a random access procedure, whether to transmit to a base station device: a first uplink message of a two-step random access procedure, or a second uplink message of a four-step random access procedure; a transmitter/receiver (220) configured, when the first uplink message of the two-step random access procedure is selected, to: transmit the selected first uplink message to the base station, and receive a random access response of the two-step random access procedure, the random access response corresponding to the transmitted first uplink message. The random access response of the two-step random access procedure is scheduled by a Physical Downlink Control Channel, PDCCH, whose Cyclic Redundancy Check, CRC, is scrambled by a first Random Access Radio Network Temporary Identifier, RA-RNTI used in the two-step random access procedure. The first RA-RNTI used in the two-step random access procedure is calculated to include a predetermined offset value for the second RA-RNTI used in the four-step random access procedure.</p>
            </abstract>
